{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>קדמת אשור</b>: The tav of קדמת stands in place of the heh. The difference between it and קדם is that the heh of קדמה stands in place of אֶל with patach, minor pathach — likewise <b>וירד אברם מצרימה</b> (Genesis 12:10), like אל מצרים. So קדמת אשור: east of Asshur. Know that from the first verse until לעשות, Scripture mentions Elohim; afterward it mentions the honored and awesome Name alongside it. How precious are the words of our early Sages of blessed memory, who said: The full Name was invoked over a full world, for there was no capacity there to receive this Name. In the pericbah of ואלה שמות I will explain the sod of the Name, if it is adjacent — if HaShem helps me. And know that the place of the earth from which man was created is near the Garden of Eden, for some say that the earth is the Land of Israel. Accept this as its force, and <b>ויהי בנסעם מקדם</b> (Genesis 11:2)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Reading 'והנח שכחו' as two words (והנח שכחו, 'accept its force'), though the phrase is elliptic and possibly textually difficult; an alternative reading 'והנה כחו' ('behold its force') appears in some witnesses."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:53.026940005Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}